\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n\nII. For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)-q(x)=q(x)-p(x).$\n\nIII. There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186360471 1071 "Let $F$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$\n- For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$\n- There are polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F$ such that $p(x)+q(x)\\ne q(x)+p(x).$" 13194139534840 17592186045417 false] [17592186360471 1071 "Let $F$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$\n\nII. For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$\n\nIII. There are polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F$ such that $p(x)+q(x)\\ne q(x)+p(x).$" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186360481 1071 "Let $U$ be the set of functions of the form $p(x)=ax,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).$\n- Multiplication by $1$ does not change elements in $U.$\n- For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" 13194139534840 17592186045417 false] [17592186360481 1071 "Let $U$ be the set of functions of the form $p(x)=ax,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).$\n\nII. Multiplication by $1$ does not change elements in $U.$\n\nIII. For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186369915 