40653 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440653 1071 "Let $D$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $r(x)=|x|,$ then $r(x)\\in D.$\n\nII. For any $f(x),g(x)\\in D,$ we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in D.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under addition." 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440653 1072 #uuid "08c8aba3-84ff-578f-a738-778ea74bd824" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440653 1074 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $r(x)=|x|\\in D$, because\n\n$$\nr(0)=|0|=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $f(x),g(x)\\in D,$ where $f(0)=0$ and $g(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nf(0)+g(0)=0+0=0.\n$$\n\nHence $f(x)+g(x)\\in D.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II it true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440654 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440651 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440654 1069 "q-106811" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440654 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440654 1071 "Let $F$ be the set of all functions $f:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ of the form $f(x)=\\frac{a}{x},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $g(x)\\in F,$ where $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2x}.$\n\nII. For any $f(x)\\in F$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot f(x)\\in F.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under scalar multiplication." 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440654 1072 #uuid "60075bc6-3e97-52cb-9240-f8444fe4b019" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440654 1074 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The set $F$ contains only functions of the form $\\frac{a}{x},$ where $a$ is a real number. The function $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2x}$ is a function of this form with $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, $g(x)\\in F.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $f(x)=\\frac{a}{x}\\in F,$ where $a\\in R,$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\nk\\cdot f(x)=k\\cdot (\\frac{a}{x})=\\frac{ka}{x}.\n$$\n\nSince $(ka)$ is a real number, we conclude that $\\frac{ka}{x}\\in F,$ i.e., $k\\cdot f(x)\\in F.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440655 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440652 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440655 1069 "q-141158" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440655 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440655 1071 "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ belongs to $T.$\n\nII. For every $A\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha \\cdot A\\in T.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under scalar multiplication." 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440655 1072 #uuid "c3d7a176-49a0-5f40-a976-fffa17513013" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true] [17592186440655 1074 "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $T$ contains only matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ However, for the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}=1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1=0≯0.$ So, ${I}_{2}\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, let $\\alpha =0\\in R$ and $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in T.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\alpha \\cdot A=0\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere the sum of the products of columns' entries is $0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0=0≯0.$ Hence, $0\\cdot A\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" 13194139534840 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0228d806-60fc-5dda-93f7-d1b0c1c47d20" 17592186440635 "answer-0bdf481d-b455-5960-ba83-4fe739f8de6f" 17592186440636 "answer-21a97d23-fb4f-5eaf-b90e-1444ccdb8660" 17592186440637 "answer-25b7f412-8325-5a8d-8ec0-efdd1fcf99b4" 17592186440638 "answer-54c85eef-42f1-5a34-b835-c200174ad259" 17592186440639 "answer-681a463d-05df-548d-8564-e21d03c83cac" 17592186440640 "answer-73d7951c-6560-5ea9-aec8-ec52869e0334" 17592186440641 "answer-957c96fc-b399-5084-82f0-23bab95940c6" 17592186440642 "answer-9f8780bf-4b01-52e4-a8c3-5d2fd02f1d5f" 17592186440643 "answer-ab50bd2a-5a75-561c-ac4e-5b893937e428" 17592186440644 "answer-ae42fca6-e22f-5cdd-ab0e-b0f6c6d5db30" 17592186440645 "answer-d1a61d10-82e9-5344-903a-035c16d02f1e" 17592186440646 "answer-d7548b7c-b486-525d-8943-136fc6cfca5d" 17592186440647 "answer-ddefe0eb-3c3f-5695-b1bd-78ac7124f1c9" 17592186440648 "answer-dfaff9c0-bcce-53cc-8481-87862075e1bb" 17592186440649 "answer-field-62c40c83-2c46-579c-a4e6-29aa8f8ba721" 17592186440650 "answer-field-89834c28-864e-52c4-81e1-b56d89beca6a" 17592186440651 "answer-field-c5e550c1-c444-5056-9fdd-7c27dc6bda79" 17592186440652 "question-08c8aba3-84ff-578f-a738-778ea74bd824" 17592186440653 "question-60075bc6-3e97-52cb-9240-f8444fe4b019" 17592186440654 "question-c3d7a176-49a0-5f40-a976-fffa17513013" 17592186440655} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
